Generate {{ num_docs }} English texts where PII appears in contexts where it normally wouldn't (recipes, technical manuals, fiction, academic papers).

## Purpose
NER models perform best in PII-heavy contexts (emails, forms). This tests detection when PII appears in unexpected contexts.

## Rules
- Mark PII entities with XML tags

## Counter-context patterns

### PII in recipes/cooking
"<PERSON>Maria Garcia</PERSON>'s family recipe, originally from the kitchen at <ADDRESS>2847 Oak Boulevard, Unit 5C, Denver, CO 80205</ADDRESS>."

### PII in technical documentation
"Manufactured by <ORGANIZATION>Siemens AG</ORGANIZATION>. Warranty contact: <PERSON>Heinrich Müller</PERSON>, <ADDRESS>Werner-von-Siemens-Straße 1, 80333 Munich, Germany</ADDRESS>."

### PII in fiction/narrative (but real-world-style)
"<PERSON>James O'Sullivan</PERSON> walked through the rain toward <ADDRESS>1423 Birch Lane, Apt 7, Eugene, OR 97401</ADDRESS>, his coat collar turned up."

### PII in academic/research text
"Study PI: <PERSON>Dr. Anita Krishnamurthy</PERSON> (<ORGANIZATION>Stanford University School of Medicine</ORGANIZATION>). Participant recruitment at <ADDRESS>300 Pasteur Drive, Palo Alto, CA 94305</ADDRESS>."

### PII in advertising
"<ORGANIZATION>Pacific Northwest Realty Group</ORGANIZATION> presents a stunning property at <ADDRESS>8700 Sunset Blvd, Suite 200, Los Angeles, CA 90069</ADDRESS>. Contact <PERSON>Sarah Mitchell</PERSON>."

### PII in Q&A/FAQ
"Q: Where should I send the return? A: Ship to <PERSON>Kevin Park</PERSON>, <ORGANIZATION>Returns Dept, Brightpath Analytics</ORGANIZATION>, <ADDRESS>2900 Corporate Drive, Suite 100, Tampa, FL 33619</ADDRESS>."

### PII in poetry/creative writing
"Born <DATE_OF_BIRTH>December 7, 1941</DATE_OF_BIRTH>, <PERSON>Eleanor Rose Patterson</PERSON> grew up by the sea."

## Confusing expressions (NO tags)
- Recipe ingredients, cooking terms
- Technical specifications ("USB 3.0", "Bluetooth 5.0")
- Fictional place names
- Statistical values ("p < 0.05", "n = 100")

## Output format
Separate each text with `---DOC_SEPARATOR---`. Each text 80-250 words.
